#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-documentation.rst:41
msgid "Summary"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-documentation.rst:43
msgid ""
"Contributions to the ROS documentation are very welcome. The ROS "
"documentation is written in reStructuredText (RST), and built using Sphinx. "
"You can find the documentation source code on `GitHub <https://github.com/"
"ros2/ros2_documentation>`__. Use the standard GitHub fork and pull request "
"(PR) workflow when making your docs contributions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-documentation.rst:48
msgid ""
"This article relates to contributing to the ROS documentation site. For more "
"information about creating or updating package documentation, see :doc:`/"
"Developer-Tools/Package-documentation/Documenting-a-ROS-2-Package`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-documentation.rst:52
msgid "Tools"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-documentation.rst:54
msgid ""
"ROS documentation is written in `reStructuredText (RST) <https://www.sphinx-"
"doc.org/en/master/usage/restructuredtext/>`__, with additional roles and "
"directives. The site is built using `Sphinx <https://www.sphinx-doc.org/en/"
"master/>`__, and more particularly using `Sphinx multiversion <https://"
"sphinx-contrib.github.io/multiversion/main/index.html>`__."
msgstr ""

