#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-documentation.rst:63
msgid "Branch structure"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-documentation.rst:65
msgid ""
"The source code of the documentation is located in the `ROS Documentation "
"GitHub repository <https://github.com/ros2/ros2_documentation>`__. This "
"repository is set up with one branch per ROS distribution to handle "
"differences between the distributions:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-documentation.rst:68
msgid ""
"If a change is common to all ROS distributions, it should be made to the "
"``rolling`` branch (and then will be backported as appropriate)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-documentation.rst:69
msgid ""
"If a change is specific to a particular ROS distribution, it should be made "
"to the respective branch."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-documentation.rst:72
msgid "Source structure"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-documentation.rst:74
msgid ""
"The source files for the site are all located under the ``source`` "
"subdirectory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-documentation.rst:75
msgid ""
"Templates for various Sphinx plugins are located under ``source/_templates``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-documentation.rst:76
msgid ""
"The root directory contains configuration and files required to locally "
"build the site for testing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-documentation.rst:79
msgid "Workflow"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-documentation.rst:81
msgid ""
"Contributors to the ROS documentation on GitHub use the standard fork and "
"pull request (PR) workflow."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-documentation.rst:83
msgid ""
"After creating your own fork of the ``ros2_documentation`` repository, clone "
"it locally, and then create a branch from the existing ``rolling`` branch "
"for your changes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-documentation.rst:84
msgid ""
"When your change to the documentation source is ready on your branch, create "
"a pull request to the upstream repository. Your PR will attract review "
"comments and suggestions from the ROS community, which you can then action "
"and agree on."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/The-ROS2-Project/Contributing/Contributing-to-documentation.rst:86
msgid ""
"When your PR is accepted, it is merged to the target branch and published to "
"the respective versions of the site."
msgstr ""

